    crm:P183i_has_representation <https://ids.lib.harvard.edu/ids/iiif/493309465/full/full/0/default.jpg> ;
    rdf:value """Monday, March 26, 1906
Motored to  Montepulciano  in a  Pour  perfectly ghastly, but young people full of fun. Scott got perfectly covered with mud to his very teeth, but wanted to go on. What it is to be young. I almost envy them. Anyhow I  love  to be with them.
Tuesday, March 27, 1906
Fine. Sun at last!
Motored to Castiglione - lunched under Chiusi - went to Orvieto via Città della Pieve. Youngsters very jolly.
Bernhard had Whiteheads to lunch.
Wednesday, March 28, 1906
Motored to Todi - then Narni, Terni, Spoleto arriving in rain. Met  Gurds  at Todi.
Bernhard called on D’Orsay and his Hungarian chanoiness Algar to dine."""^^xsd:string ;
    mbdiaries-ontology:index 64 ;
    mbdiaries-ontology:part_of <https://mbdiaries.itatti.harvard.edu/resource/diary/1906> .

